# Location and Maps Rules

- Use the provider abstraction selected in `/flutter/docs/09-location.md`.
- Request location permissions explicitly and handle denied/restricted states.
- Do not continuously track outside documented operational need.
- Validate location samples for availability and accuracy before using them operationally.
- Cache/map data required for active offline deliveries when the provider supports it.
- Never expose a driver's private continuous location outside authorized delivery context.
- Handle GPS disabled, poor accuracy, mock/stale locations, permission revocation, and battery constraints gracefully.
- Location events must contain timestamps and be associated with the correct delivery/driver context when applicable.
